            "review_title": "Review at Pink Moment Cafe",
            "review_text": "Jackie Hua\nSan Diego, California3 contributions\n1\ngood spot for chilling in this hustling town\nJan 2020 • Solo\nDecided to gave this coffee a try while wandering around Tan Dinh Church even though it’s relatively new. When I first came in, I had noticed the AC so strong that immediately gave me a pleasant cool feeling after being under the sun all day, that’s a bonus point. Also, the Café itself has a bright and welcoming atmosphere, rooftop with panoramic church view and very attentive staffs. Last but not least, I like how they presented “Cafe Sua Da” with the pink coffee phin filter, it was very creative and fun, which later my friends asked me a lot about this picturesque cafe when they saw my story. Highly recommended if you’re in town and in need of a chill vibe Café.\nRead more\nWritten February 20, 2020",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-13",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
