            "review_title": "Review at Pink Moment Cafe",
            "review_text": "go4theglobe\nSeattle, Washington285 contributions\n1\nFriendly staff, cute atmosphere with the best view of the pink church\nFeb 2020\nI hopped into the Pink Moment Cafe purely to take photos of the Tan Dinh Church (pink church) across the street at sunset after my friend and I found out we weren't able to go inside the church (it is under construction). The third floor balcony has a great view of the church! We took a ton of photos from there. The atmosphere is really cute too.\n\nCiders were two for 85,000 so my friend and I each got a cider (get the berry cider if you want a pink drink!). \n\nThe staff member helping us was very friendly and patient. We arrived a little before 6pm (I believe they are supposed to close at 6) and he came upstairs and told us they were closing at 6:30 (so I think he extended it for us?).\n\nThey have WiFi and a lot of power outlets. I didn't use the WiFi so I'm not sure how good it is but it seemed like it would be a great place to hang out and work if needed.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten February 15, 2020",
